From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:52:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: a longer budget for the first parse of a file

Problem: one 500 ms budget covers both the first parse of a file and the
update after each edit. On AROS (x86_64 under QEMU TCG) the first parse of
a 230 KB Rust file (helix-term/src/commands.rs, 6825 lines) timed out, so
the file opened without highlighting.
Change: on AROS the first parse may take 3 s. Updates after edits keep
500 ms: for that file they took 0.3-1.0 s each (depending on the boot), so a
longer update budget would keep highlighting at the price of that lag per
keystroke; with 500 ms a slow update switches highlighting off for the
buffer, as upstream does. A 27 KB file updated in 0.05-0.11 s.
Repository: helix-editor/helix
Base: a05c151bb6e8e9c65ec390b0ae2afe7a5efd619b (tag 25.07.1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: target_os = "aros"; other targets unchanged.
Upstream status: local-only (not submitted).
Verification: guest timings from a diagnostic build (timing logs) on AROS
One 1.3, pool v11-1, three boots; guest clocks under TCG run at a varying
rate, so the figures are guest time. With 3 s the 230 KB file opened
highlighted in two boots (Syntax::new 1.4 s and 4.5 s including queries).
---
 helix-core/src/syntax.rs | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/helix-core/src/syntax.rs b/helix-core/src/syntax.rs
index 8fa185c6f..daa476257 100644
--- a/helix-core/src/syntax.rs
+++ b/helix-core/src/syntax.rs
@@ -430,7 +430,23 @@ pub struct Syntax {
     inner: tree_house::Syntax,
 }
 
+#[cfg(not(target_os = "aros"))]
 const PARSE_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_millis(500); // half a second is pretty generous
+#[cfg(not(target_os = "aros"))]
+const UPDATE_PARSE_TIMEOUT: Duration = PARSE_TIMEOUT;
+
+// AROS (x86_64, measured under QEMU TCG): the first parse of a 230 KB Rust
+// file timed out at 500 ms and the file opened without highlighting. With a
+// 3 s budget it parsed in both boots measured (Syntax::new, queries
+// included, took 1.4 s and 4.5 s of guest time). Opening may wait that long once. Edits keep the upstream budget: an
+// update of that file took 0.3-1.0 s per keystroke, and a longer budget
+// would keep the highlighting at the price of that lag; with 500 ms a slow
+// update switches highlighting off for the buffer instead. A 27 KB file
+// updated in 0.05-0.1 s.
+#[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
+const PARSE_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(3);
+#[cfg(target_os = "aros")]
+const UPDATE_PARSE_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_millis(500);
 
 impl Syntax {
     pub fn new(source: RopeSlice, language: Language, loader: &Loader) -> Result<Self, Error> {
@@ -449,7 +465,7 @@ pub fn update(
         if edits.is_empty() {
             Ok(())
         } else {
-            self.inner.update(source, PARSE_TIMEOUT, &edits, loader)
+            self.inner.update(source, UPDATE_PARSE_TIMEOUT, &edits, loader)
         }
     }
 
